 ## Overview
 This method is a GPU-based volume rendering technique for data compressed via run-length encoding, specifically targeting voxelized models with sharp or small details [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently accessing massive voxel grids ($1000^3$ and larger) by storing only surface voxels uncompressed while compressing inside and outside voxels, achieving compression ratios up to 1:20 for noise-free data [S1]. Unlike methods that require full decompression, this approach distinguishes between uncompressed surface voxels and compressed interior/exterior regions on-the-fly during ray casting, avoiding the overhead of reconstructing the full volume in memory [S1].
